@*
    REQ-UI-051 (BRD-167, BRD-164..BRD-166) — the Playbook axis of `/misses`, rendering real figures
    (docs/mockups/misses-playbook.html).

    The mockup this is built to is a POPULATED axis. BRD-126's `PlaybookEmpty` is still what shows when
    no Playbook miss records have been imported for the signed-in user — it is a condition of the data,
    no longer the permanent shape of the axis.

    Six things here are deliberate and are not stylistic:

      1. Every guarded figure comes off `PlaybookMissReport`, which the engine computes under the
         Playbook's OWN guards (PlaybookMissGuards) — stricter than the TechieFlow stream's and never
         relaxed to match it. This file re-computes none of them.
      2. `found_phase_gate` (process) and `found_gate` (assertion) are rendered as two side-by-side
         columns that are never summed, merged or charted together; `item_id` and `req_id` are two
         columns on one table. Same rule, same reason, as `phase_gate` versus `gate` (BRD-165).
      3. There is no "unknown model" row on the model band and there never will be. The records the
         guard refused are counted BY REASON — a claim about the data — beside it (BRD-166).
      4. Cost is three cohorts and never one number: sole (measured headline) · shared:n (apportioned,
         separately labelled) · none (a count, never a divisor). `PlaybookCostSplit` carries no blended
         member, so no control here can bind one (ADR-019).
      5. Every denominator sits BESIDE its figure: `n of N assessed` on the why_missed card's face, the
         attribution exclusion under the origin cross-tab, the cohort counts under each cost card.
      6. Nothing is grouped by `actor`. The field is provenance, never an axis (BRD-168).

    The lifecycle, rework and time-to-close figures are not on the report type — they are the same
    read of `VerdictAfter` / `Reopened` the TechieFlow engine makes (BRD-120), applied to the folded
    Playbook records here, and every one of them goes through `Figure` so a comparison under three
    records renders `insufficient data (n=…)` and never a zero.
*@
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text.Json
@using TfLens.Core.Metrics
@using TfLens.Core.Playbook

<div class="pb-misses-surface tflens-stack" data-testid="pb-misses-surface">

    @* BRD-164 — where these rows came from and what they upsert on, stated on the page. *@
    <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Info" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="pb-miss-ingest-note">
        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
        <AlertTitle>Framework is a provenance axis, and it never pools</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
            These figures come from the Playbook's committed
            <span class="font-mono">verification/telemetry/misses.ndjson</span>, normalized by its own
            exporter and imported through <b>Import metric files</b> — into the <b>same</b>
            <span class="font-mono">Miss</span> / <span class="font-mono">MissFix</span> /
            <span class="font-mono">MissAmend</span> tables, with no second ingest path. Nothing here
            shares a figure, a series or a total with the TechieFlow axis. Records upsert on the
            <b>immutable source-line hash</b>, not on the TechieFlow natural keys, because re-export is
            expected and stream order is part of the record.
        </AlertDescription>
    </Alert>

    @if (MissCount == 0)
    {
        @* BRD-126 — a condition of the data, not the permanent shape of this axis. *@
        <PlaybookEmpty />

        <Card data-testid="misses-playbook-plan">
            <CardHeader>
                <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                        <CardTitle Class="text-base">What this axis renders once a bundle is imported</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>
                            The same bands as the TechieFlow axis, plus the two cross-edition axes the
                            Playbook carries and TechieFlow does not. The switch changes the data, never
                            the layout or the rules.
                        </CardDescription>
                    </span>
                    <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">BRD-167</Badge>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                    <table class="pb-table">
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var vBand in PlannedBands)
                            {
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="text-muted-foreground">@vBand.Band</td>
                                    <td>@vBand.Detail</td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
            <CardFooter>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="misses-playbook-zero-note">
                    A zero here is <b>absence, not a good score</b>. Nothing is rendered as a figure until
                    there are records behind it, and no comparative figure below
                    @MetricsConstants.MinN records is ever printed as a number. TfLens holds
                    @MissCount Playbook miss records for this window.
                </p>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>

        @* Absence is stated as absence, on the same card the populated state uses. *@
        <Card data-testid="pb-stream-health">
            <CardHeader>
                <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                        <CardTitle Class="text-base">Playbook stream health</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>From Coverage — nothing here is a quality figure</CardDescription>
                    </span>
                    <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">records held</Badge>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                    <table class="pb-table" aria-label="Playbook miss streams held for this user">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Stream</th>
                                <th class="pb-num">Records</th>
                                <th class="pb-num">Newest</th>
                                <th>State</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var vStream in StreamRows)
                            {
                                <tr data-testid="@($"pb-stream-{vStream.Kind}")">
                                    <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vStream.Kind</span></td>
                                    <td class="pb-num">@vStream.RecordsText</td>
                                    <td class="pb-num text-xs">@vStream.NewestText</td>
                                    <td>
                                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" Class="@vStream.BadgeClass">@vStream.State</Badge>
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
            <CardFooter>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="pb-stream-health-note">
                    A zero or a dash here is <b>absence, not a good score</b>.
                    <span class="font-mono">events</span> is <b>transient and best-effort</b> — it is the
                    exporter's input, rotates, and TfLens never stores it, so its absence is not an error.
                </p>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>
    }
    else
    {
        @* ── BAND 1 — lifecycle and the figures the guards bound ───────────────────────── *@
        <div class="tflens-stack" data-testid="miss-kpis">
            <div class="pb-kpi-row">
                <StatGroup Columns="4">
                    <StatTile Title="Backlog (open now)"
                              Value="@Text(Lifecycle.Open)"
                              Description="@BacklogDetail"
                              IconName="bug"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Destructive"
                              data-testid="kpi-open" />
                    <StatTile Title="Closed"
                              Value="@Text(Lifecycle.Closed)"
                              Description="@ClosedDetail"
                              IconName="circle-check"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart2"
                              data-testid="kpi-closed" />
                    <StatTile Title="Reopened"
                              Value="@Text(Lifecycle.Reopened)"
                              Description="closed then reopened at least once — its own count, never folded into open or closed"
                              IconName="refresh-cw"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart4"
                              data-testid="kpi-reopened" />
                    <StatTile Title="Time to close — median / p90"
                              Description="@TimeToCloseDetail"
                              IconName="clock"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart5"
                              data-testid="kpi-time-to-close">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <span class="pb-pair">
                                <FigureText Value="@MedianTimeToCloseHours"
                                            Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(MedianTimeToCloseHours)"
                                            TestId="kpi-time-to-close-median" />
                                @if (MedianTimeToCloseHours.HasValue)
                                {
                                    <span class="pb-unit">h</span>
                                }
                                <span class="pb-slash">/</span>
                                <FigureText Value="@P90TimeToCloseHours"
                                            Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(P90TimeToCloseHours)"
                                            TestId="kpi-time-to-close-p90" />
                                @if (P90TimeToCloseHours.HasValue)
                                {
                                    <span class="pb-unit">h</span>
                                }
                            </span>
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                </StatGroup>
            </div>

            <div class="pb-kpi-row">
                <StatGroup Columns="4">
                    <StatTile Title="Design-miss share"
                              Description="@DesignShareDetail"
                              IconName="book-open"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart3"
                              data-testid="kpi-design-share">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@DesignMissShare"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(DesignMissShare)"
                                        TestId="kpi-design-share-value" />
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                    <StatTile Title="Escape share (misses)"
                              Description="@EscapeShareDetail"
                              IconName="triangle-alert"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart2"
                              data-testid="kpi-escape-share">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@EscapeShare"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(EscapeShare)"
                                        TestId="kpi-escape-share-value" />
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                    <StatTile Title="Rework incidence"
                              Description="@ReworkDetail"
                              IconName="activity"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                              data-testid="kpi-rework-incidence">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@ReworkIncidence"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(ReworkIncidence)"
                                        TestId="kpi-rework-incidence-value" />
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                    @* The one headline repair figure, and the only one entitled to be called the cost of
                       a repair: sole AND a complete valid window AND cost_status complete (BRD-166). *@
                    <StatTile Title="Measured repair tokens"
                              Description="@HeadlineTokensDetail"
                              IconName="database"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                              Class="pb-measured"
                              data-testid="kpi-rework-tokens">
                        <TitleAdornment>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"
                                   Class="pb-measured-badge"
                                   data-testid="kpi-rework-tokens-badge">sole · complete</Badge>
                        </TitleAdornment>
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@Report.Cost.HeadlineTokens.Sole"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(Report.Cost.HeadlineTokens.Sole)"
                                        TestId="kpi-rework-tokens-value" />
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                </StatGroup>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* BRD-166 — the guard, in words, always on the page rather than in a tooltip. *@
        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="pb-miss-guard-note">
            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>
                The Playbook's reporting guards are stricter than the TechieFlow stream's, and they are
                not relaxed to match it
            </AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>
                A model or tier attribution requires <span class="font-mono">origin_confidence: "linked"</span>
                <b>and</b> a complete valid source window <b>and</b> a non-null observed model. A headline
                repair token or cost figure additionally requires
                <span class="font-mono">cost_attribution: "sole"</span> and
                <span class="font-mono">cost_status: "complete"</span>. An <b>inferred or unknown origin is
                never placed in an “unknown model” bucket</b> — a bucket named for a model is a claim about
                a model, and these records do not support one.
            </AlertDescription>
        </Alert>

        @* ── BAND 2 — where misses come from ──────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <TypographyH2 Class="text-lg">Where misses come from</TypographyH2>
        <div class="pb-grid pb-grid-origin">

            <Card data-testid="miss-origin">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Origin command phase × miss class</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Did we specify badly, or build badly?</CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">attributed only</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (OriginRows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-origin-none">
                            No miss in this window clears the attribution guard, so there is no per-origin
                            figure to state. That is an absence of attribution, not a zero — the reasons are
                            counted below.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                            <table class="pb-table pb-table-origin" aria-label="Misses by origin command phase and miss class">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Origin phase</th>
                                        @foreach (var vClass in OriginClasses)
                                        {
                                            <th class="pb-num">@vClass</th>
                                        }
                                        <th class="pb-num">Total</th>
                                        <th class="pb-num">Executions</th>
                                        <th class="pb-num">Per 100 executions</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    @foreach (var vRow in OriginRows)
                                    {
                                        <tr data-testid="@($"miss-origin-{vRow.Phase}")">
                                            <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Phase</span></td>
                                            @foreach (var vClass in OriginClasses)
                                            {
                                                <td class="pb-num">@vRow.CountOf(vClass)</td>
                                            }
                                            <td class="pb-num font-semibold">@vRow.Total</td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">@(vRow.Executions is { } vRuns ? vRuns.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) : Missing)</td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">
                                                <FigureText Value="@vRow.Rate" Class="text-xs" />
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    }
                                    <tr data-testid="miss-origin-unattributed">
                                        <td class="text-muted-foreground">excluded from attribution</td>
                                        @foreach (var vClass in OriginClasses)
                                        {
                                            <td class="pb-num text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                        }
                                        <td class="pb-num font-semibold">@Report.Attribution.RefusedN</td>
                                        <td class="pb-num text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                        <td class="pb-num text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                    </tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    }
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    @* BRD-166 / BRD-121 — the exclusion is on the page, always, even at zero, and it names
                       a property of the DATA rather than of whoever produced it. *@
                    <p class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-taint-count">
                        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="14" />
                        <span>
                            <b>@Report.Attribution.RefusedN of @MissCount misses excluded</b> from every
                            per-origin figure@(RefusalBreakdown(Report.Attribution.Refused)). The
                            @Report.Attribution.AttributedN that remain cleared all three conditions.
                            An exclusion the reader cannot see is indistinguishable from a bug.
                        </span>
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>

            <Card data-testid="miss-whymissed">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Which practice failed</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>
                                Is our <b>specification</b> weak, or our <b>verification</b>?
                            </CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        @* BRD-166 — the denominator is on the card's face, never a tooltip. *@
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"
                               Class="tflens-badge-warning"
                               data-testid="miss-whymissed-denominator">
                            @Report.WhyMissedAssessed
                        </Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (PracticeRows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-whymissed-none">
                            No miss in this window carries <span class="font-mono">why_missed</span>. A
                            <span class="font-mono">null</span> means <i>not assessed</i> — it is not a
                            bucket, not an <span class="font-mono">other</span>, and not a zero.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                            <table class="pb-table" aria-label="Failed-practice distribution over misses that carry why_missed">
                                <tbody>
                                    @foreach (var vRow in PracticeRows)
                                    {
                                        <tr data-testid="@($"miss-whymissed-{vRow.Practice}")">
                                            <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Practice</span></td>
                                            <td class="pb-bar">
                                                <Progress Value="@vRow.SharePercent" Class="w-16" />
                                            </td>
                                            <td class="pb-num text-xs">@vRow.Count · @vRow.Share</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    }
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    }
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-whymissed-eligibility">
                        @WhyMissedFooter
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* ── BAND 2b — the two cross-edition axes, side by side and never merged ───────── *@
        <div class="pb-grid pb-grid-2">

            <Card data-testid="miss-found-axes">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Where it was caught — two axes, never one</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>
                                A <b>process</b> gate and an <b>assertion</b> gate are different measurements
                            </CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">@MissCount records</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                        <table class="pb-table" aria-label="found_phase_gate and found_gate, reported as two separate axes">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs">found_phase_gate</span>
                                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">process</Badge>
                                    </th>
                                    <th class="pb-num">Misses</th>
                                    <th>
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs">found_gate</span>
                                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">assertion</Badge>
                                    </th>
                                    <th class="pb-num">Misses</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var vRow in FoundAxisRows)
                                {
                                    <tr>
                                        <td>
                                            @if (vRow.PhaseGate is { } vPhaseGate)
                                            {
                                                <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vPhaseGate</span>
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                <span class="text-muted-foreground">@Missing</span>
                                            }
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="pb-num">@(vRow.PhaseGateCount?.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) ?? Missing)</td>
                                        <td>
                                            @if (vRow.Gate is { } vGate)
                                            {
                                                <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vGate</span>
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                <span class="text-muted-foreground">@Missing</span>
                                            }
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="pb-num">@(vRow.GateCount?.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) ?? Missing)</td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="text-muted-foreground">no process gate on the record</td>
                                    <td class="pb-num">@NoPhaseGateCount</td>
                                    <td class="text-muted-foreground">no assertion gate on the record</td>
                                    <td class="pb-num">@NoGateCount</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-found-axes-note">
                        These two columns are <b>side by side and never summed, merged or charted
                        together</b> — the same rule, and the same reason, as
                        <span class="font-mono">phase_gate</span> versus <span class="font-mono">gate</span>.
                        A process gate says <i>which stage of the method caught it</i>; an assertion gate
                        says <i>which check fired</i>. Adding them would count one miss twice and mean
                        nothing.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>

            <Card data-testid="miss-id-axes">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Item identity across editions</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>One axis under two names — two columns on one table</CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">normalized</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                        <table class="pb-table" aria-label="item_id beside req_id">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th><span class="font-mono text-xs">item_id</span> <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">(Playbook)</span></th>
                                    <th><span class="font-mono text-xs">req_id</span> <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">(TechieFlow)</span></th>
                                    <th class="pb-num">Misses</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var vRow in Report.ByItemId)
                                {
                                    <tr data-testid="@($"miss-item-{vRow.Key}")">
                                        <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Key</span></td>
                                        <td class="text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                        <td class="pb-num">@vRow.Count</td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="text-muted-foreground">no item recorded</td>
                                    <td class="text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                    <td class="pb-num">@NoItemIdCount</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-id-axes-note">
                        <span class="font-mono">req_id</span> stays empty on Playbook records and
                        <span class="font-mono">item_id</span> stays empty on TechieFlow ones. Two columns,
                        one table — collapsing them into a single “ID” column would erase which edition
                        the identifier belongs to.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* ── BAND 3 — who was running ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <TypographyH2 Class="text-lg">Who was running</TypographyH2>

        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="pb-miss-observational">
            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>Observational only — this band does not show causation</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>
                Miss counts per model are confounded by <i>which model gets the hard work</i>. Read these
                as a description of what ran, not as a ranking. Computed from the
                <b>@Report.Attribution.AttributedN records</b> that clear all three conditions:
                <span class="font-mono">origin_confidence: "linked"</span>, a complete valid source window,
                and a non-null observed model.
            </AlertDescription>
        </Alert>

        <div class="pb-grid pb-grid-2">
            <Card data-testid="miss-origin-model">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">By origin model</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Miss rate per linked origin model</CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">@Report.Attribution.AttributedN eligible</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (ModelRows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-origin-model-none">
                            No record clears the model guard, so no bucket may be named for a model. The
                            records that did not clear it are counted by reason above, never under a name
                            that would read as a model's score.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                            <table class="pb-table" aria-label="Misses by origin model, attributed records only">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Model</th>
                                        <th class="pb-num">Misses</th>
                                        <th class="pb-num">Executions</th>
                                        <th class="pb-num">Per 100 executions</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    @foreach (var vRow in ModelRows)
                                    {
                                        <tr data-testid="@($"miss-model-{vRow.Key}")">
                                            <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Key</span></td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">@vRow.Count</td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">@(vRow.Executions is { } vRuns ? vRuns.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) : Missing)</td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">
                                                <FigureText Value="@vRow.Rate" Class="text-xs" />
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    }
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    }
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-origin-model-note">
                        There is <b>no “unknown model” row</b> on this table and there never will be. The
                        @Report.Attribution.RefusedN records that do not clear the guard are counted in the
                        exclusion line above, not bucketed under a name that would read as a model's score.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>

            <Card data-testid="miss-origin-tier">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">By origin tier</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Same guard, same exclusions</CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">@Report.Attribution.AttributedN eligible</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (TierRows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-origin-tier-none">
                            No attributed record carries an <span class="font-mono">origin_tier</span>. The
                            tier is a producer field preserved in the record's overflow; where it is absent
                            the band is empty rather than filled with a guess.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                            <table class="pb-table" aria-label="Misses by origin tier, attributed records only">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Tier</th>
                                        <th class="pb-num">Misses</th>
                                        <th class="pb-num">Share</th>
                                        <th>Dominant class</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    @foreach (var vRow in TierRows)
                                    {
                                        <tr data-testid="@($"miss-tier-{vRow.Key}")">
                                            <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Key</span></td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">@vRow.Count</td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">
                                                <FigureText Value="@vRow.Share" Class="text-xs" />
                                            </td>
                                            <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Dominant</span></td>
                                        </tr>
                                    }
                                    @if (TierMissing > 0)
                                    {
                                        <tr data-testid="miss-tier-missing">
                                            <td class="text-muted-foreground">tier missing on the record</td>
                                            <td class="pb-num">@TierMissing</td>
                                            <td class="pb-num text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                            <td class="text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    }
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    }
                </CardContent>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* ── BAND 4 — cost of rework, three cohorts that never merge ──────────────────── *@
        <TypographyH2 Class="text-lg">Cost of rework</TypographyH2>
        <div class="pb-grid pb-grid-3" data-testid="miss-cost">

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="miss-cost-measured">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Measured</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>
                                <span class="font-mono">sole</span> + complete window +
                                <span class="font-mono">cost_status: complete</span>
                            </CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <span class="pb-chip pb-chip-2 shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="circle-check" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="pb-money tabular-nums">
                        <FigureText Value="@Report.Cost.HeadlineTokens.Sole"
                                    Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(Report.Cost.HeadlineTokens.Sole)"
                                    TestId="miss-cost-sole" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                        output tokens per miss repaired · @Report.Cost.HeadlineRecords
                        @(Report.Cost.HeadlineRecords == 1 ? "fix" : "fixes") whose window covered exactly
                        this item and whose provider cost is complete. <b>This is a measurement.</b>
                    </p>
                    <div class="pb-rule">
                        <Separator />
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Measured USD (opencode)</span>
                        <span class="font-semibold tabular-nums" data-testid="miss-cost-measured-usd">@MeasuredUsdDisplay</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-cost-measured-basis">
                        @MeasuredUsdBasis
                    </p>
                </CardContent>
            </Card>

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="miss-cost-apportioned">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Apportioned</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription><span class="font-mono">cost_attribution: shared:n</span></CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <span class="pb-chip pb-chip-4 shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="pb-money tabular-nums">
                        <FigureText Value="@Report.Cost.HeadlineTokens.Apportioned"
                                    Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(Report.Cost.HeadlineTokens.Apportioned)"
                                    TestId="miss-cost-apportioned-value" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                        output tokens per miss, divided equally across @Report.Cost.ApportionedRecords
                        @(Report.Cost.ApportionedRecords == 1 ? "fix" : "fixes") that each repaired several
                        misses. One window over several misses — <b>arithmetic, not measurement</b>, and
                        never summed into the column beside it.
                    </p>
                    <div class="pb-rule">
                        <Separator />
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Divided equally, and we say so</span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"
                               Class="tflens-badge-warning"
                               data-testid="miss-cost-apportioned-label">apportioned</Badge>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-cost-apportioned-usd-note">
                        No apportioned <b>dollar</b> figure is published beside it: a measured
                        <span class="font-mono">cost_usd</span> belongs to a whole repair window, and
                        dividing it would put an estimate in the same unit as a measurement.
                    </p>
                </CardContent>
            </Card>

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="miss-cost-unattributable">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Unattributable</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription><span class="font-mono">cost_attribution: none</span></CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <span class="pb-chip pb-chip-danger shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="x" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="pb-money tabular-nums" data-testid="miss-cost-none">
                        @Report.Cost.ExcludedRecords
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                        fixes with <b>no numbers at all</b> — no distinct repair window, or a window the
                        producer will not vouch for. A count, never a divisor. Missing beats invented.
                    </p>
                    <div class="pb-rule">
                        <Separator />
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-cost-refusals">
                        @CostRefusalLine
                    </p>
                </CardContent>
            </Card>
        </div>

        <p class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-cost-no-blend">
            <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="14" />
            <span>
                There is no blended figure on this page, in the export or in parity — measured and
                apportioned repair cost never share a series, a total or an aggregate, and
                <span class="font-mono">none</span> is excluded rather than divided into.
                <span class="font-mono">PlaybookCostSplit</span> carries no property a blend could bind to
                (ADR-019).
            </span>
        </p>

        @* ── Diagnostics — what the ingest could not apply, and what it holds ─────────── *@
        <div class="pb-grid pb-grid-2">

            <Card data-testid="miss-amend-diagnostics">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Amendment &amp; orphan diagnostics</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>
                                Surfaced here and on Coverage — never applied or discarded silently
                            </CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">re-folded at read time</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                        <table class="pb-table" aria-label="Amendment and orphan diagnostics">
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var vRow in DiagnosticRows)
                                {
                                    <tr data-testid="@($"miss-diagnostic-{vRow.Key}")">
                                        <td>@vRow.Label</td>
                                        <td class="pb-num font-semibold">@vRow.Count</td>
                                        <td class="pb-note text-xs text-muted-foreground">@vRow.Note</td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-amend-diagnostics-note">
                        Duplicate source lines are an <b>ingest-time</b> diagnostic — a re-exported line
                        that has not changed upserts onto the same row — and are counted where the import
                        happens, on Coverage. In the healthy case every count here is zero; a non-zero one
                        means TfLens and the producer disagree about the same file.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>

            <Card data-testid="pb-stream-health">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Playbook stream health</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>From Coverage — nothing here is a quality figure</CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <span class="pb-chip pb-chip-5 shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="activity" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                        <table class="pb-table" aria-label="Playbook miss streams held for this user">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Stream</th>
                                    <th class="pb-num">Records</th>
                                    <th class="pb-num">Newest</th>
                                    <th>State</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var vStream in StreamRows)
                                {
                                    <tr data-testid="@($"pb-stream-{vStream.Kind}")">
                                        <td><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vStream.Kind</span></td>
                                        <td class="pb-num">@vStream.RecordsText</td>
                                        <td class="pb-num text-xs">@vStream.NewestText</td>
                                        <td>
                                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" Class="@vStream.BadgeClass">@vStream.State</Badge>
                                        </td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="pb-stream-health-note">
                        A zero or a dash here is <b>absence, not a good score</b>.
                        <span class="font-mono">events</span> is <b>transient and best-effort</b> — it is
                        the exporter's input, rotates, and TfLens never stores it, so its absence is not an
                        error. When no Playbook miss records have been imported at all, this page shows the
                        <span class="font-mono">PlaybookEmpty</span> state instead — that state is a
                        condition, not the permanent shape of this axis.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* ── Per-miss detail ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <Card data-testid="miss-detail">
            <CardHeader>
                <div class="flex w-full flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                        <CardTitle Class="text-base">Every miss</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>
                            @DetailRows.Count @(DetailRows.Count == 1 ? "record" : "records") · amendments
                            folded at read time, so a <span class="font-mono">why_missed</span> supplied
                            later shows here
                        </CardDescription>
                    </span>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                <div class="pb-scroll-x">
                    @* TR-009: InitialPageSize is set explicitly — the grid truncates to it even when
                       pagination is off, so it is never left at the default 5. *@
                    <DataTable TData="DetailRow"
                               Data="@DetailRows"
                               ShowToolbar="true"
                               ShowPagination="true"
                               InitialPageSize="25"
                               AriaLabel="Every Playbook miss in this window"
                               data-testid="miss-detail-table">
                        <Columns>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.MissId)" Header="Miss">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.MissId</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.ItemId)" Header="item_id">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.ItemId</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.ReqId)" Header="req_id">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">@vRow.ReqId</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.MissClass)" Header="Class">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.MissClass</span></Badge>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Severity)" Header="Severity">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <Badge Variant="@vRow.SeverityVariant">@vRow.Severity</Badge>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Origin)" Header="Origin">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1">
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Origin</span>
                                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">@vRow.Confidence</Badge>
                                    </span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.FoundBy)" Header="Found by">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="text-xs">@vRow.FoundBy</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.FoundPhaseGate)" Header="found_phase_gate">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.FoundPhaseGate</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.State)" Header="Lifecycle">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <Badge Variant="@vRow.StateVariant">@vRow.State</Badge>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="DetailRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Tokens)" Header="Repair tokens"
                                             CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-1">
                                        <span class="tabular-nums text-xs">@vRow.Tokens</span>
                                        @if (vRow.Attribution is { Length: > 0 })
                                        {
                                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">@vRow.Attribution</Badge>
                                        }
                                    </span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                        </Columns>
                    </DataTable>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What an absent fact renders as — never a blank, never a zero.</summary>
    private const string Missing = "—";

    /// <summary>What a record that names no origin phase is grouped under.</summary>
    private const string PhaseNotNamed = "not named";

    /// <summary>What a record that carries no <c>miss_class</c> is shown as.</summary>
    private const string ClassNotRecorded = "not recorded";

    /// <summary>The producer's tier field, preserved in each record's overflow rather than a column.</summary>
    private const string OriginTierKey = "origin_tier";

    /// <summary>The lifecycle word for a miss no fix has closed.</summary>
    private const string OpenState = "opened";

    /// <summary>The lifecycle word for a miss whose latest verdict is <c>Verified</c>.</summary>
    private const string ClosedState = "closed";

    /// <summary>The lifecycle word for a miss that was closed and opened again.</summary>
    private const string ReopenedState = "reopened";

    /// <summary>The lifecycle word for a miss that was declined; never folded into open.</summary>
    private const string DeclinedState = "wont-fix";

    /// <summary>What the bands describe on an axis holding no records yet.</summary>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<PlannedBand> PlannedBands =
    [
        new PlannedBand("Band 1 — lifecycle",
            "backlog · closed · reopened · median and p90 time to close, then design-miss share · escape share · rework incidence and intensity · measured repair tokens"),
        new PlannedBand("Band 2 — Where misses come from",
            "origin command phase × miss class with the attribution exclusion beneath it, beside the why_missed distribution and its n of N assessed denominator"),
        new PlannedBand("Band 2b — The two cross-edition axes",
            "found_phase_gate (process) beside found_gate (assertion), never summed; item_id beside req_id, two columns on one table"),
        new PlannedBand("Band 3 — Who was running",
            "origin model and origin tier over attributed records only, with no unknown-model bucket and the refusal reasons stated"),
        new PlannedBand("Band 4 — Cost of rework",
            "measured (sole + complete window + cost_status complete) · apportioned (shared:n) · unattributable (none), rendered as three cohorts and never as one"),
        new PlannedBand("Diagnostics and detail",
            "amendment and orphan diagnostics, the streams held, and every miss with both identity axes in their own columns")
    ];

    private PlaybookMissReport objReport = EmptyReport;
    private Dictionary<string, List<MissFixRecord>> objFixesByMiss = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    /// <summary>The stored <c>miss</c> rows for the selected window, unfolded and in stream order.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<MissRecord> Misses { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The stored <c>miss-fix</c> rows for the selected window.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<MissFixRecord> Fixes { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The stored <c>miss-amend</c> rows for the selected window, folded at read time.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<MissAmendRecord> Amends { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>
    /// The Playbook run records for the window, if any — the denominator of a per-execution rate.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Optional on purpose. The Playbook's own effort stream lives in its phase tables rather than in
    /// <c>runs</c>, so this list is routinely empty; a rate with no denominator renders
    /// <c>—</c> through <see cref="Figure"/> rather than a fabricated zero.
    /// </remarks>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<RunRecord> Runs { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The guarded report every figure on this surface is read off.</summary>
    private PlaybookMissReport Report => objReport;

    /// <summary>Misses in the window, after amendments were folded.</summary>
    private int MissCount => objReport.Misses.Count;

    /// <summary>The lifecycle counts, read the way BRD-120 reads them.</summary>
    private LifecycleCounts Lifecycle { get; set; } = new(0, 0, 0, 0);

    /// <summary>Hours between a miss and the repair that closed it, one per closed miss.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<double> ClosureHours { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>Fix records per miss that drew at least one repair.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<double> ReworkCounts { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>An empty report, so the surface never binds a <c>null</c> before its first parameters.</summary>
    private static PlaybookMissReport EmptyReport { get; } =
        PlaybookMissNormalizer.Read(FrameworkNames.Playbook, [], [], []);

    /// <summary>Median hours to close, refused below the minimum-n floor.</summary>
    private Figure MedianTimeToCloseHours =>
        Hours(ClosureHours, aValues => MetricsConstants.Median(aValues));

    /// <summary>p90 hours to close, refused below the minimum-n floor.</summary>
    private Figure P90TimeToCloseHours => Hours(ClosureHours, aValues => Percentile(aValues, 0.90));

    /// <summary>Misses whose <c>miss_class</c> says the requirement was never written down.</summary>
    private Figure DesignMissShare =>
        Share(
            objReport.Misses.Count(aMiss =>
                string.Equals(aMiss.MissClass, MissFigures.DesignMissClass, StringComparison.Ordinal)),
            MissCount);

    /// <summary>Misses that reached a human before any gate caught them.</summary>
    private Figure EscapeShare =>
        Share(
            objReport.Misses.Count(aMiss =>
                aMiss.FoundBy is not null
                && MissFigures.EscapeFoundBy.Contains(aMiss.FoundBy, StringComparer.Ordinal)),
            MissCount);

    /// <summary>Misses that drew at least one repair, over every miss in the window.</summary>
    private Figure ReworkIncidence => Share(ReworkCounts.Count, MissCount);

    /// <summary>Median repairs per reworked miss — the intensity beside the incidence.</summary>
    private Figure ReworkIntensity =>
        ReworkCounts.Count switch
        {
            0 => Figure.NotApplicable(),
            < MetricsConstants.MinN => Figure.InsufficientData(ReworkCounts.Count),
            _ => Rounded(MetricsConstants.Median(ReworkCounts)!.Value, ReworkCounts.Count)
        };

    /// <summary>The sub-line under the backlog tile, which names what is inside the count.</summary>
    private string BacklogDetail =>
        $"latest lifecycle state is {OpenState} or {ReopenedState} · deferred is counted here, "
        + $"{DeclinedState} never is ({Lifecycle.Declined} declined)";

    /// <summary>The sub-line under the closed tile.</summary>
    private string ClosedDetail =>
        $"of {MissCount} recorded {(MissCount == 1 ? "miss" : "misses")} · read from the latest repair "
        + "verdict, never inferred from the presence of a fix";

    /// <summary>The sub-line under the time-to-close tile.</summary>
    private string TimeToCloseDetail =>
        $"miss-fix.ts − miss.ts over {ClosureHours.Count} closed "
        + $"{(ClosureHours.Count == 1 ? "miss" : "misses")}, in hours";

    /// <summary>The sub-line under the design-miss-share tile.</summary>
    private string DesignShareDetail =>
        $"{MissFigures.DesignMissClass} over all {MissCount} misses — the spec itself omitted it";

    /// <summary>The sub-line under the escape-share tile, which says which escape figure this is.</summary>
    private string EscapeShareDetail =>
        $"found_by ∈ {{{string.Join(", ", MissFigures.EscapeFoundBy)}}} over {MissCount} misses — "
        + "NOT the gates-derived escape rate on Gate outcomes";

    /// <summary>The sub-line under the rework tile, carrying the intensity beside the incidence.</summary>
    private string ReworkDetail =>
